@meta
id: 22-09
title: Normal-mode keys on the selection
chapter: 22
type: lesson
skills: visual-line
par: 43
minutes: 5
vscode: Alt+click before each `, ctx`, Shift+End, Left, Delete
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Chapter 15 gave you `:g/pattern/normal keys`: a loop of normal-mode
keystrokes over every line that matches. The range from a selection
drives the same loop without a pattern. `:'<,'>normal keys` runs the
keys once on each selected line, cursor at the start of the line each
time.

The logger in `cancel` no longer takes a context argument. Remove
`, ctx` from every log call in `cancel`. The calls are different
lengths, so the comma is in a different column on each line; the one in
`markShipped` keeps its `ctx` for now.

@keys
| `:'<,'>normal keys` | run `keys` in normal mode on each selected line |
| `f,` | find the comma |
| `dt)` | delete up to the closing bracket |

@hints
On one line, by hand, you would do `f,dt)`. That is the keys sequence.
The selection decides which lines get it.
--
Select the body of `cancel`, not its signature — the signature has a
comma too. From the first line of the body, `Vi{` takes the lines
between the method's braces. Then `:`, the range appears, then
`normal f,dt)`.
--
`/async cancel` `Enter`, `j`, `Vi{`, `:normal f,dt)` `Enter`. Lines
with no comma are skipped: `f,` fails, and a failed key stops that
line's sequence without touching it.

@solution
    /async cancel<Enter> j V i { :normal f,dt)<Enter> :wq<Enter>

Thirty-six keystrokes. `:s/, ctx)/)/` would also have done it, and on
this file it is the shorter answer. Reach for `:normal` when the edit
is positional rather than textual — "the second argument", "after the
first comma", "the last word" — because a normal-mode sequence already
knows how to say those things and a regex has to be taught.

The fact that `f,` failing aborts the rest of the line is a feature.
It means a `:normal` over a loosely chosen region only ever touches the
lines the first key can find something on. The flip side is that `f,`
finds the *first* comma, whatever it is in. Had one of the messages
contained a comma, that line would have been cut in the wrong place,
and the signature line — which also has a comma — is exactly why the
selection starts one line down.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { Logger } from '../../infrastructure/logger';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(Logger) protected logger: Logger,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string, ctx: RequestContext) {
    this.logger.info('cancel requested', ctx);
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
    if (!order) {
      this.logger.warn('cancel of unknown order', ctx);
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }
    this.logger.info('refunding', ctx);
    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    this.logger.info('refund complete', ctx);
    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async markShipped(id: string, ctx: RequestContext) {
    this.logger.info('markShipped', ctx);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { Logger } from '../../infrastructure/logger';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(Logger) protected logger: Logger,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string, ctx: RequestContext) {
    this.logger.info('cancel requested');
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
    if (!order) {
      this.logger.warn('cancel of unknown order');
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }
    this.logger.info('refunding');
    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    this.logger.info('refund complete');
    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async markShipped(id: string, ctx: RequestContext) {
    this.logger.info('markShipped', ctx);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}
